# OpenSpec generates its codex command surface with `openspec init --tools codex`
# (core spec §16 bind-upstream: generated per host by the CLI, never a vendored
# artifact maintained by hand). The spec slot itself (openspec/) IS committed —
# only the regenerable command surface is ignored.
.codex/skills/openspec-*/
.gstack/

# Core's artifacts are PINNED, not vendored (ADR-0047). bin/ is a cache
# regenerated from tools/core-vendor.manifest by bin/materialise-core-artifacts.sh
# and hash-verified against it. Never committed: a committed copy is a copy that
# drifts, and these two spent a release stale at gate 1.3.1 / wrapper 1.1.0.
bin/openspec-change-gate.sh
bin/reviewer-cli.sh
